  "while_flat_a_true_entry_refusal": 3,
  "while_holding_residual": 39,
  "why_removal_is_not_automatic": "on these same cycles the shell would mostly have EXTENDed -- bought more of the side already held, in markets whose bid was falling. COMPLETE and EXTEND must be decided separately, never netted.",
  "why_this_matters": "entry_band_left is an ENTRY admission band. A firing while holding unmatched inventory refuses a residual action, not an entry."
 },
 "flow_hypothesis": "SUPPORTED IN THE PARTIAL COHORT, UNTESTABLE IN THE ZERO COHORT. Entry spread is 0.010 at the median in every cohort and four FULL-cover markets show bid drift as violent as the stranded ones, so the static book features we recorded do not separate FULL from ZERO -- there, our own abandonment dominates the variance and no market property could show through it. The PARTIAL cohort is the clean case FOR the hypothesis: 141 COMPLETE orders, 47 per market, worked for up to 43 minutes, and a 5.7% fill rate. That is a market that will not transact against a resting maker, measured after persistence is ruled out as the cause. The campaign did not record the feature that would name it -- contemporaneous trade prints and two-sided print rate are not in the order rows, only spread, touch extrema and poll counts. Naming it needs a forward collector that tapes prints per market; the baseline it must beat is in this file.",
 "labels": {
  "counterfactual": "did not happen; fill-assumed, queue position and depth not modelled",
  "descriptive": "cohorts are not randomly assigned; no causal claim is made",
